> On Sep 3, 2024, at 4:42 PM, Maxim Fortun <max@maxf.net> wrote:
>=20
> Based on feedback from Kirk and Colin I added configuring the parser =
class name via server.properties, added some tests, and updated the docs =
to reflect this.
> I find the config file name by re-parsing the command line. If anyone =
knows a better way of passing KafkaConfig to static initialization, I'd =
appreciate a nudge in the right direction. It's not the most efficient =
way of retrieving configs, but it is done only once at load time, so the =
overhead should be negligible while providing a consistent location for =
all configs. I have also left the system prop and env ways of passing =
this config in. Hopefully this is ok and is not considered a code bloat.
>=20
