Hi TengYao,
Thanks for the KIP. From my point of view, calling Producer#flush in a call=
back is a
bad idea and it would be better to disallow it.

AS1: If we are tightening up the rules about which Producer methods can be =
called
in the callback, I wonder whether some other methods should be treated in t=
he
same way. It seems to me that it is unwise to change the transactional stat=
e of the
producer in a callback, so I would also prohibit Producer#initTransactions.

I wonder what others think about begin/commit/abortTransaction also.

Thanks,
Andrew
