> * Create a new section in the {{README.md}} file titled "Kafka Components" (or similar).
>  * Create a table using Markdown with the following columns: Component, Description, Link.
>  * Populate the table with the core Kafka components and add links to the relevant sections of the official Kafka documentation for each component.
>  ** *Brokers:* Servers that store and manage Kafka topics and partitions.
>  ** *Topics:* Categories or feeds of records.
>  ** *Partitions:* Subdivisions of a topic that allow for parallel processing and distribution of data.
>  ** *Producers:* Clients that publish records to Kafka topics.
>  ** *Consumers:* Clients that subscribe to Kafka topics and process records.
>  ** *Connect:* A framework for connecting Kafka with external systems (databases, message queues, etc.).
>  ** *Streams:* A library for building stream processing applications with Kafka.
>  * Format the table for readability and clarity.



