On 12/5/24 11:28 AM, Divij Vaidya wrote:
> ## Validations (on AArch64 machine)
> 
> 1. Built from source
> 2. Ran all tests (successful amongst multiple runs)
> 3. Verified basic produce/consume
> 4. Verified that the maven artifacts contain 3.7.2 bits
> 
> ## Problems
> 
> 1. While checking the commits on the branch, I found one commit which is
> not captured in release notes (
> https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17190). I have updated the JIRA
> with the correct tag now. This does not require a new RC.
> 
> 2. Do we want to backport changes to 3.7 such as
> https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18051 and
> https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17062? The former is a
> good-to-have validation and the latter impacts data stored by Tiered
> Storage which is not GA in 3.7. Hence, we do not need a new RC, but if we
> do end up creating one for a different reason, let's backport these.
> 
> ## Vote
> 
> + 1 (binding)
> 
> --
> Divij Vaidya
