Beatriz Aparecida de Freitas Rodrigues created KAFKA-18171:
--------------------------------------------------------------

             Summary: Unexpected Change in bootstrap.servers Behavior After=
 Upgrade to 3.8.0
                 Key: KAFKA-18171
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18171
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: config
    Affects Versions: 3.8.0
         Environment: Operating system: windows 11
Kafka Version: 3.8.0 =C2=A0
Previous Version: 3.7.0 =C2=A0
Configuration:=C2=A0=C2=A0
=C2=A0 =C2=A0- `bootstrap.servers: "140.2.15.25:9092 140.2.15.26:9092 140.2=
.15.27:9092"` =C2=A0
            Reporter: Beatriz Aparecida de Freitas Rodrigues


After upgrading from Kafka version *3.7.0* to 3.8.0, I encountered an issue=
 with the configuration of the `bootstrap.servers` property. =C2=A0

In previous versions, it was possible to configure the `bootstrap.servers` =
with space-separated URLs, like this: =C2=A0


{code:java}
bootstrap.servers: "140.2.15.25:9092 140.2.15.26:9092 140.2.15.27:9092"=20
{code}
=C2=A0


However, with version {*}3.8.0{*}, this configuration results in the follow=
ing exception: =C2=A0

=C2=A0
{code:java}
org.apache.kafka.common.config.ConfigException: Invalid url in bootstrap.se=
rvers: 140.2.15.25:9092 140.2.15.26:9092 140.2.15.27:9092 {code}
=C2=A0

=C2=A0

The configuration only works correctly if the URLs are separated by commas,=
 as shown below: =C2=A0

=C2=A0
{code:java}
bootstrap.servers: "140.2.15.25:9092,140.2.15.26:9092,140.2.15.27:9092" {co=
de}
=C2=A0

=C2=A0

This behavior appears to be a change from previous versions where space-sep=
arated URLs were accepted. =C2=A0

*Reproducible Example:*
To demonstrate the issue, I created a minimal project that reproduces the p=
roblem. You can find it here: =C2=A0
[GitHub Repository|https://github.com/BeatrizRodrigues/kafka-config-test]

*Question:* =C2=A0
Is this the expected behavior for version *3.8.0* ? Was support for space-s=
eparated `bootstrap.servers` values intentionally deprecated, or is this a =
bug introduced in the latest release? =C2=A0



Looking forward to clarification on whether this is an intentional change o=
r a bug. Thank you!



