Calvin MongoDB created KAFKA-18175:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Breaking change for SystemTime usages
                 Key: KAFKA-18175
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18175
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 3.9.0
            Reporter: Calvin MongoDB


Kafka version 3.9 introduced a breaking change by disallowing SystemTime in=
stantiations.=C2=A0

https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-16879

=C2=A0

To quote the original ticket KAFKA-16879

> Howerver,=C2=A0 system time is unique=EF=BC=8CIn an application, the time=
 obtained in different places should be consistent,=C2=A0 But now the time =
obtained by using the Java System class to interact with the underlying lay=
er is the same=E3=80=82

=C2=A0

I'm not sure we should have introduced a breaking change for these reasons.=
 Also, why do we believe that the time would be different across instantiat=
ions of `new SystemTime()` if under the hood they're only calling System me=
thods `return System.currentTimeMillis();`?

=C2=A0

Additionally, I suspect that forcing the singleton pattern with SystemTime =
might also negatively impact usage patterns around `waitObject`, what if so=
meone wants to have multiple waitObject calls running in parallel? Which th=
ey would only be able to do with separate instantiations of SystemTime.

=C2=A0

>From MongoDB's perspective it is a fairly simple change for us to just go a=
head and reference the singleton, but I just wanted to callout that I suspe=
ct this may cause more issues for others.



--
