Hello,

I=E2=80=99d like to propose a feature enhancement for the kafka-client =
java library, where implementors can choose a custom HostResolver =
implementation.

Rationale: we=E2=80=99re currently connecting to a Kafka broker that we =
don=E2=80=99t control, running in a Windows server environment. This =
server lists its own machine host name in `advertised.listeners` rather =
than an IP address. This would normally be fine, except that this name =
isn=E2=80=99t registered in DNS in our target environment - in fact =
there are no local DNS servers. Since we intend to replicate this setup =
in many locations, it becomes cumbersome to also replicate a DNS server =
just to serve this one name (that will be different in each location). =
Instead, we plan to use a custom HostResolver implementation that uses a =
3rd party library (jcifs-ng) to do the lookup over SMB.

Proposal: add a `hostname.resolver` optional configuration property =
specifying a class to use as the HostResolver implementation. If not =
specified, it defaults to DefaultHostResolver. This would be similar to =
other configuration options such as `metric.reporters` and =
`key.deserializer`.

I=E2=80=99ve created a branch that implements this, but there=E2=80=99s =
no associated JIRA ticket and I don=E2=80=99t have access to create one. =
Should I do that?

Thank you!=

