Hi folks,

Happy feature freeze day! Please remember that the big chunks of your KIPs
must be merged by today. In practice, I plan to cut the release branch on
Monday so you have a few more days. If you cannot make it, please reachout
to me to discuss how to proceed. I will go and remove the KIPs which are
not ready from the release plan on Monday too.

Alyssa/Colin:
Thanks for reaching out to me about KIP-966. It seems to me that
https://github.com/ahuang98/kafka/pull/2 is a pretty large change for after
the feature freeze. How do you quantify the risk? Do we have a way back in
case we cannot make it or if we discover issues?

Andrew/Divij:
Thanks!

Luke:
Good catch! I also stumbled upon it yesterday. Let's wait for Ismael.

Best,
David

