I think KIP-1087 is actually "done".

The linked Jira ticket might just be wrong. The KIP proposes to 
deprecate `--intermediate-topic` options in AK 4.0, and we did add a 
WARN log for it via:

  - 
https://github.com/apache/kafka/commit/05696037d330e5e355d62cb1b977bac9df78db82
  - 
https://github.com/apache/kafka/commit/a9eb06bbdf9b3d14736223edc1e3650677e2fe6d

The linked open Jira of the KIP is actually to *remove* the option and 
it is of course for 5.0. For KIPs we usually call them "done" when the 
deprecation ships, not after we finally remove something.

Should we link https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-12823 for the 
KIP instead, as the code for the warn log was merged with this ticket?


-Matthias


